--TEST--
`queryAs<T>` over a class with an inline-shape field is refused while compiling rather than once per row — `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`, `rule:core-classes/derive-field-list`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/db-column-types` makes a row a flat list of columns, so a
// nested document is not one. The property is answered twice, and the two say
// different things: the declaration carries a type the map has no row for, and
// the *call* has a constructor parameter no column can fill. Only the second
// is a question about the call, which is why it waits for the whole program —
// the class is routinely declared in a file the walk has not reached — and it
// is `nvs_types::derive`'s `check_row_sites` that answers it after the walk.
//
// This is the refusal that used to be said once per row. `Core\Db\Row`'s
// `hydrate` still carries it as the backstop for a class built by hand, where
// there is no `#[Db\Derive]` for a compiling pass to read.
use Core\Db\Transaction;

#[Core\Db\Derive]
class Row {
    public int $n;

    public {city: string} $where;

    public function constructor(int $n, {city: string} $where)
    {
        $this->n = $n;
        $this->where = $where;
    }
}

class Rowsource {
    public static function all(Transaction $tx): Core\Db\Rows<Row>
    {
        return $tx->queryAs<Row>("select n, city from t", []);
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0756]: `Row::$where` is declared `{city: string}`, which has no column mapping
%A
error[E0806]: `Row::$where` is declared a type no column reads back, so `Core\Db\Transaction::queryAs` has no value to give it
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
